    "rdma_unknown_rate_bps": 5000000000.0,
    "rdma_unknown_comment": "per-QP cap for RDMA flows the executor has no budget for yet (mailbox 0xccf); the DPA applies rate per QP, so a 4-QP flow-set gets 4x this",
    "d_star_s": 0.003,
    "trust_recover_s": 1.0,
    "conf_comment": "law=conf = design v4 (hpft_design_v4.md, 2026-08-28): receiver root = (port - unscheduled arrival)(1-h), two water-fillings (share; lenders demand A(1+delta) but keep E = share), virtual queue Q <- clip(Q + A - E, 0, D E), feedback {q = Q/E in periods} (no direction bit: the sender probes whenever q = 0); sender R <- R exp(alpha min(m, m_max)) (m = consecutive empty-queue feedbacks; the step grows with the silence, alpha = alpha_max/m_max) exp(-kappa dq) (dq signed while a queue exists) exp(-(kappa/D) q), the probe bounded by R <- max(R, min(R e^step, min(maxrate, r_cap_mult x own send rate))); executors blend r = T cc + (1-T) R with executor-owned trust (decay by q/D, rise only while the CC is binding: TCP cwnd-limited 100 ms, RDMA cc below 98% level and not rising over 100 epochs); kappa 0.01 / D 300 (zeta 0.87) chosen for a loop delay of 40-60 feedbacks plus the executor's own lag (offline model); PERIOD 10 ms (= one meter round, 2026-08-29): per-feedback constants are the 1 ms ones scaled by the period (kappa 0.1 linearly, D 30 unchanged, alpha 3e-4 quadratically since it is the growth rate of the step; alpha_max = alpha m_max = 3%, overshoot alpha_max tau ~ 9%); the trust epoch in the executors stays 1 ms",
